      "summary": "Solves an Atari control task with Generative Adversarial Imitation Learning, replacing standard convolutional feature extraction with Sharpened Cosine Similarity layers for lower-noise feature detection. Combines an AlphaGo-style policy/value approach with a GAN-like discriminator, blending inverse RL cost extraction with RL policy learning; a genuinely novel research combination with 8 stars.",
      "excerpt": {
        "type": "code",
        "text": "def forward(self, inputs):\n    # Reshape the input tensor\n    x = inputs.view(-1, self.flat_size, self.channels * self.kernel_size ** 2)\n\n    # Normalize the input and weight tensors\n    x_norm = self.l2_normal(x, axis=2)\n    w_norm = self.l2_normal(self.w, axis=1)\n\n    # Compute cosine similarity\n    x = torch.matmul(x / x_norm, self.w / w_norm)\n\n    # Apply sharpening function\n    sign = torch.sign(x)\n    x = torch.abs(x) + 1e-12\n    x = torch.pow(x + self.b ** 2, torch.sigmoid(self.p) * F.softplus(self.p))\n    x = sign * x\n    x = x.view(-1, self.output_y, self.output_x, self.units)\n    return x",
        "source": "src/prod/SharpCosSim2D.py",
        "why": "A from-scratch PyTorch Sharpened Cosine Similarity layer: L2-normalizes signal and kernel to compute true cosine similarity, then applies a learnable sign-preserving sharpening exponent, a subtle numerically-careful reimplementation of a non-standard conv alternative."
      },
