      "summary": "Reference implementation for a research paper comparing philosophical frameworks (individual fairness, social/utilitarian, and Rawlsian veil-of-ignorance/maximin) as distinct LLM allocation agents, evaluated across static, dynamic, and cultural scenarios with equity, welfare, and Gini metrics. A rigorous multi-agent fairness study operationalizing moral philosophy in code.",
      "excerpt": {
        "type": "code",
        "text": "def maximin_decision(options, outcomes):\n    \"\"\"Implements the maximin decision principle\"\"\"\n    if not options or not outcomes or len(options) != len(outcomes):\n        raise ValueError(\"options and outcomes must be non-empty and same length\")\n\n    worst_outcomes = [min(scenario) for scenario in outcomes]\n    best_index = np.argmax(worst_outcomes)\n    return options[best_index], worst_outcomes[best_index]",
        "source": "src/fairness_mas/agents/veil_allocator.py",
        "why": "Directly encodes Rawls' veil-of-ignorance maximin rule (maximize the worst-case outcome) as the decision core of an anonymous fairness agent, a crisp translation of a philosophical principle into a decision function."
      },
