      "summary": "A pip-installable CLI utility that extracts text from many file types (PDF, DOCX, XLSX, CSV, TXT, MD, TEX), clusters documents by content similarity with automatic k selection via the elbow method, and sorts them into keyword-named folders. A clean, shipped, real-world NLP tool.",
      "excerpt": {
        "type": "code",
        "text": "def elbow_method(distance_matrix: np.ndarray, max_clusters: int = 10) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Determine the optimal number of clusters using the elbow method.\"\"\"\n    max_clusters = min(max_clusters, n_samples - 1)\n    wcss = []\n    for i in range(1, max_clusters + 1):\n        kmeans = KMeans(n_clusters=i, init='k-means++', max_iter=300,\n                        n_init=10, random_state=0)\n        kmeans.fit(distance_matrix)\n        wcss.append(kmeans.inertia_)\n    elbow_point = np.argmin(differences) + 1\n    return min(elbow_point + 1, n_samples)",
        "source": "document_sorter/main.py",
        "why": "Automatic cluster-count selection via the elbow method with sensible guards against degenerate small-sample cases, letting the tool sort documents with zero user tuning."
      },
